Z||000000||Gold-86SE||07-01-2000||12:35 AM||||<BR>Well, we are beginning our trip to pick up the new Fiero.<P>We will be starting out from San Antonio near 7 am and driving up to the Dallas area, this should make for a fun weekend.<P>I just hope that no dope decides to take me out this weekend.<P>I'll let you guys know how it went when I get back.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)||||reg||6
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||07-05-2000||11:20 AM||||<BR>Thought I would update you guys on the July 4th weekend road trip to pick up my new Fiero.<P>The trip lasted Saturday thru Tuesday, we stayed with my brother and his wife, and it wore me out, glad I could go back to work to get some rest.<P>The traffic was good for us, for we were headed North on IH35, but those poor saps headed South, man were they in for a long ride, I guess everyone was headed for the coast. Heading South it was stop-n-go traffic as far as the eye could see, in at least six separate locations. Traffic coming home was good, but heavy, for everyone, now, was headed North.<P>On the road my wife and I saw three Fieros. A white notchback, either an 85GT or 86SE, very nice, very clean.  The second was a sport coupe (I think) and somebody had no love for it, it was dirty and nasty looking.  The third was a 85 or 86 coupe, dead red paint.  As the guy passed us, he saw the Fiero sitting on the trailer and we waved at each other, which was kinda cool.<P>The other Fieros (about 20, give or take 3) we saw were in a storage location were I bought my Fiero. He has several 88's, more fastbacks, and a bunch of notches.  I was informed that he primarily sells Fieros to those individuals who want and will put them back on the road.  If you are interested I am sure I can let you have his information.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)||||reg||7
Z||000002||pollock||07-05-2000||11:48 AM||||Was that Continental Auto Salvage in Ft. Worth? <P>I'm in Denton... need a few things for my Fiero.<P>BTW, i was one of those poor southbound schlepps you saw on Friday.  I bailed off of 35 in Waco and take 77 the rest of the way to Port Aransas.  Wasn't in my Fiero, though.  Thank God.  That would have been a shitty drive.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gold-86SE||07-05-2000||02:09 PM||||<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pollock:<BR><B>Was that Continental Auto Salvage in Ft. Worth? <P>I'm in Denton... need a few things for my Fiero.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>This place was a residence and owned by an individual and he is located near McKinney, Northeast of Dallas.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dan86gt3.8||07-05-2000||06:23 PM||||Man if I had known you guys were rolling through waco I would have try and met y'allsomewhere.  But I was ato work monday and teusday afternoon and I didn't get close to I-35 so i don't know what it looked like.  Is it possible that you bought a fiero from a guy thats a member of north texas fiero's.  I have talked to the guy and aparently he has 32 fieros in a fenced in location near his house.  I hav talked to him online before, pretty cool guy.  Ithink he is about to putt in an lt1 into a car.  Anywyas sorry I missed this thread, and have a great time with your new ride.  Besides I am stripping mine to paint right now so its not too much to look at.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Gold-86SE||07-06-2000||10:11 AM||||<BR>Dan, I believe we are talking about the same guy.  And yes he mentioned that he is going to do a V8 conversion on a blue 87 t-top. The cars are in his back yard and man does he have a collection.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)||||reg||1
